sec.p:
ZnO particle size distributions in the range of 0.01–1000 μm were determined with the use of Mastersizer 3000 (Malvern Instruments Co., Ltd., UK). The sample preparation was carried out in a wet unit (Hydro EV) in which a powder material was dispersed in distilled water. The results of the analysis provided the following parameters:
D[3.2]—Sauter mean diameter, which is an average of particle size;
D[4.3]—De Brouckere mean diameter, which is a volume mean diameter;
d(0.1)—10% of the particles have diameters smaller than the specified value;
d(0.5)—a median of particle distribution, i.e., 50% of the particles have higher and another 50% of the particles have lower diameters than this value;
d(0.9)—90% of the particles have diameters smaller than the specified value.
